# MigrationsPurpose:  Track and execute project migrations after .sdd/ schema updates.  Migrations ensure project instances stay consistent with the current  .sdd/ structure and conventions.Owns: ./ReadOrder:   1 @INDEX.sdd   2 @../INDEX.sdd   3 @../../commands/sdd-migrate.sddRules:  [MIG1] Migrations MUST be applied in order (001, 002, 003, ...).  [MIG2] Each migration MUST be tracked as pending, applied, or failed.  [MIG3] Failed migrations MUST halt the pipeline until resolved.  [MIG4] Migrations MUST be idempotent — safe to run multiple times.  [MIG5] Rollback MUST restore the previous state before the migration.  [MIG6] Migrations MUST be documented with before/after descriptions.Migration Lifecycle:  PENDING -> APPLIED  PENDING -> FAILED -> (fix) -> PENDING -> APPLIED  APPLIED -> ROLLED_BACK (only if migration supports rollback)State: +